          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "घाट — ghāṭ — \"a ghat, steps down to a river\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माफ़ कीजिए, घाट कैसे जाते हैं? māf kījiye, ghāṭ kaise jāte haiṁ? Excuse me, how do I get to the ghat?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "घाट (ghāṭ) goes back to Sanskrit ghaṭṭa, \"a landing place\" (CDIAL 4414): the steps where people come down to bathe."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
